    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The integration strategy for construction pairs two layers (BAI weekly, 00:15:57\u201300:22:09):\n\n- **Speckle** (open-source) manages low-level, industry-specific 3D data \u2014 synchronizing models across Revit, Blender, AutoCAD, with a robust, mature ecosystem. It handles details like door counts or piping data.\n- **Powerhouse document models** sit at the high level \u2014 project management, requirements, approvals \u2014 referencing the low-level data.\n\nThe payoff: documents automatically update when the underlying 3D models change, delivering value **without requiring clients to replace their existing software stacks** (00:17:17).\n\nDiligence notes (BIM briefing):\n- Speckle's server is partially enterprise-licensed \u2014 the Apache vs enterprise boundary needs mapping (speckle-server repo; specklepy's IFC handling includes per-file licenses)\n- Under the hood Speckle partially uses **ifcopenshell** for IFC work, so the open toolchain remains reachable if Speckle's licensing becomes a constraint\n\nThis is the general shape of the positioning: don't compete with mature low-level tools \u2014 compose with them and own the document/process layer above.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-14T18:13:42.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T18:13:42.000Z"
    }
